generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/checker — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal contract.
// Directory-shared-scope package (25 files): the type checker's builtin
// signature tables (builtins.vibe + 13 builtins_*.vibe lookup_* modules),
// the core expression/statement checker (checker.vibe, checker_stmt.vibe),
// pattern checking + exhaustiveness (checker_pattern.vibe,
// checker_exhaustive.vibe), type-expr resolution (checker_resolve.vibe), and
// the effect/mutability discipline passes (checker_effects.vibe — see
// relocation note below). checker_facade.vibe (see naming note below)
// re-exports a SUBSET of the surface (lookup_builtin, check_expr,
// check_pattern, pat_has_unsupported_or_binding, resolve_type_expr,
// CheckedProgram, check_program, check_program_result,
// check_program_type_table, check_program_with_env,
// check_program_with_env_result, check_stmts,
// canonical_retained_trait_impl_entries_snapshot, canonical_retained_trait_method_gens_snapshot, canonical_checked_type_defs_snapshot, canonical_checked_value_env_snapshot, canonical_effective_value_env_snapshot, and the narrowly scoped type-definition observation APIs) via the `export ./file.vibe { names }`
// SReExport form (#726);
// every other name below is defined directly (`export fn`) in its own
// sibling file and reaches outside importers purely through this package's
// directory-shared scope + the facade generated from THIS contract (not
// from checker_facade.vibe's own hand-written re-export list, which the
// generated facade supersedes at ingestion time) — same shape as
// codegen/expr's expr.vibe/core.vibe/support.vibe split.
//
// Naming-collision note: the established rename convention for this
// migration batch is `git mv index.vibe <dirname>.vibe` (see
// codegen/expr/expr.vibe, codegen/gc/gc.vibe, syntax/syntax.vibe). For this
// directory the dirname is "checker", but `checker/checker.vibe` already
// exists as a substantial (5.3k line) real implementation file — the core
// expression checker, not a facade — so `git mv index.vibe checker.vibe`
// would silently clobber it. `validate_index_layout_fs` also forbids
// index.vibe and index.vpkg coexisting in the same directory ("a boundary
// has exactly one index"), so leaving index.vibe in place unrenamed was not
// an option either (loader/index.vibe::desugar_contract_source_fs). The old
// index.vibe was therefore renamed to `checker_facade.vibe` instead —
// non-colliding, and its content did not need any other change: directory
// auto-discovery (`contract_sibling_impl_raws`) already reaches every other
// sibling file regardless of what checker_facade.vibe itself re-exports, so
// the facade file's existing partial re-export list stays correct as-is.
//
// checker_effects.vibe relocation note: this file used to live at
// lib/@vibe/compiler/checker_effects.vibe (a sibling of the checker/
// directory, not inside it) specifically so `checker/checker_stmt.vibe`
// (which needs check_perform_effects_stmts_env etc. from it) could import it
// as a "#847 Phase C exception" direct leaf import, deliberately bypassing
// checker's own facade — routing that import through the facade would close
// a real cycle (checker package -> checker_stmt.vibe -> checker_effects.vibe
// -> checker package). Once checker/ became a real `index.vpkg` package
// boundary, `enforce_incoming_boundary_fs` (#729) rejected that same direct
// leaf import from OUTSIDE the package ("cannot import ... across a package
// boundary"), since checker_effects.vibe itself was not a checker/ member —
// and routing it through the package (the boundary-legal alternative)
// reintroduced the exact cycle the leaf import had been added to avoid
// (confirmed empirically: `type_db: import cycle detected at
// checker/index.vpkg`). Moving checker_effects.vibe INTO checker/ resolves
// both constraints at once: checker_stmt.vibe's own need for it becomes an
// ordinary same-package sibling import (no facade indirection, no cycle),
// and every outside consumer (entry/compiler/file_compile/file_compile.vibe,
// several tests) now reaches its surface through this contract like any
// other checker export. EffectError is declared transparently (bodyless,
// no `opaque` keyword) rather than opaque, matching common_base's structs:
// several tests pattern-match its constructors directly (e.g.
// `EEEffectfulCallOutsideEffect(_) => true`), so the declaration only
// attests name + arity while checker_effects.vibe's real enum definition
// stays the single source of truth callers actually see.
//
// Compiled into the compiler itself via compiler_sources_manifest.tsv
// (group `checker`): the old single `checker/index.vibe` row becomes a
// dual row (this contract + checker_facade.vibe); the former top-level
// `checker_effects.vibe` row is repointed to `checker/checker_effects.vibe`;
// every other impl file in this directory already had its own manifest row
// before this migration and is unchanged.

